Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: rockchip-vaapi
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         libva2,
         librockchip-mpp1
Description: VA-API driver for Rockchip RK3588 via MPP
 Hardware video acceleration driver that bridges the VA-API (libva)
 interface to Rockchip MPP (librockchip-mpp1) for the RK3588/RK3576 SoC.
 .
 Enables validated H.264 and VP9 hardware decode via DRM PRIME 2 DMA-BUF
 surface export. Experimental HEVC and 10-bit profiles remain opt-in.
 .
 Install rockchip-vaapi-config or select the driver per application.

Package: rockchip-vaapi-config
Architecture: all
Depends: rockchip-vaapi (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: system environment for the Rockchip VA-API driver
 Optional system-wide environment files that select the Rockchip VA-API
 driver and allow GStreamer's va plugin to probe its non-Intel vendor string.
 .
 This package does not disable browser sandboxes or force browser display
 backends. Those settings must be handled per application.
